# Code revision: e5075bfe

## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.fillProcessQueueInfo(null)` acquires its read lock,
encounters and catches the null dereference, then releases the lock and returns
normally. Rust previously required a mutable info reference and could not
represent the null input. It now exposes `fill_process_queue_info_nullable`,
which forwards a present info value and does nothing for `None`.

The invoked Java facade fixture records the normal return, and the Rust facade
comparison calls the nullable method. Fixture SHA-256:
`57e2890ebeace93ecf00e2509e2bf7557c28f681ad19141f81430fecfe57ddf3`.

## Commits

- `e5075bfe fix(consumer): preserve null ProcessQueue info behavior`.
